A||||1||80's BOY||Auto tranny shift kit interchange???||||5||
Z||000000||80's BOY||06-21-2001||05:56 PM||||I am taking out my 85 6cyl tranny to put in a 4cyl tranny in its place. I installed a shift kit from the Fiero store last year. If I exchange the throttle body and plates from the old tranny, along with the governor assembly, would there be any problems?Are these parts interchangeable?? I hope they are, so I won't have to do all the tedious work for another shift kit.||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||06-21-2001||07:38 PM||||You need to be very carefull with that. The valve body of the TH125 had a bunch of changes over the years. Some are easier to detect than others. I think there are about 3 "major" versions of the valve body but there can be small changes that may cause issues.<P>You might be able to swap the body as a whole unit but don't count on it. check them very carefully.<P>It would be safer to put another kit into the replacement. You can also get the kits--&gt;<A HREF="http://www.txchange.com/" TARGET=_blank>Transmission Exchange Co.</A> I think the price might be better. You can get any other parts you need from them as well.||||reg||1
